AffectedWorkspacesInWindow(openedWindow, promptReason.workspaceName);\n420:       break;\n421:     }\n422:     case 'CLOSE_OTHER_WINDOWS': {\n423:       const windowsToClose = openedWindows.filter((window) => window.windowName !== promptReason.windowNameToSpare);\n424:       affectedWorkspaces = windowsToClose.flatMap((w) => getAffectedWorkspacesInWindow(w));\n425:       break;\n426:     }\n427:   }\n428: \n429:   return showClosePrompt(affectedWorkspaces);\n430: }\n431: \n432: /**\n433:  * Prompts for confirmation to close the workspaces with unsaved changes in the given window: the whole\n434:  * window, or, if `upToWorkspaceName` is given, just that workspace and its children. Unlike\n435:  * `promptForClosingWorkspaces`, this works on any window, including one held in an\n436:  * `<ExportedWorkspace>`'s local store.\n437:  * @returns a Promise that resolves to true if the user confirmed, or there was nothing to confirm.\n438:  */\n439: export function promptForClosingWorkspacesInWindow(\n440:   openedWindow: OpenedWindow,\n441:   upToWorkspaceName?: string,\n442: ): Promise<boolean> {\n443:   return showClosePrompt(getAffectedWorkspacesInWindow(openedWindow, upToWorkspaceName));\n444: }\n445: \n446: /**\n447:  * Closes the named workspace, along with its children, within the given window.\n448:  * @returns the updated window; `null` if no workspaces are left in it; or `openedWindow` itself if\n449:  *   the workspace is not in the window.\n\n(Showing lines 390-449 of 735. Use offset=450 to continue.)\n</content>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"08e0a29d-87a4-4811-b406-56a5d5f7f8de","uuid":"e1010712-7229-4873-bc0e-09f5d92d06d0","timestamp":"2026-10-20T04:07:14.320Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"<repo>github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core</repo>\n<path>packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/workspace2.ts</path>\n<url>undefined</url>\n<content>\n390:  *\n391:  * This function prompts the user for confirmation to close workspaces w