{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgCq7K8ZSRbjA8TaNLWiB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Short answer:** `launchWorkspace2(workspaceName, workspaceProps, windowProps, groupProps)` in `esm-styleguide` checks the target workspace's window and group, then opens the workspace. Whenever an open group, window, or workspace has props that don't match, it asks the user to confirm closing the conflicting part. If they confirm, the old state is discarded and the requested workspace is opened in a fresh window. Declining returns `false` and leaves everything unchanged.\n\n**Opening a workspace with props.** `launchWorkspace2` (`workspace2.ts:133`) throws if the workspace isn't registered or isn't attached to a window and group. Props are compared with `arePropsCompatible` (`workspace2.ts:333`): two sets are compatible if either is null, or if they are shallow-equal. The documented behaviour is in `launchWorkspace2.md`.\n\n**Conflicting group (`workspace2.ts:165-190`).** If a different group is open, or the same group has incompatible group props, the code prompts with `CLOSE_WORKSPACE_GROUP`. On confirm it replaces `openedGroup` and sets `openedWindows` to a single window holding the new workspace. The group-switch prompt is called with `explicit: true`, so only workspaces with unsaved changes are listed. `launchWorkspaceGroup2.md` documents this with `explicit: false`, so the docs and code differ on which workspaces the prompt lists.\n\n**Conflicting window (`workspace2.ts:191-240`, `241-272`).**\n- If the window is open with compatible window props but the workspace is open with incompatible workspace props, it prompts with `CLOSE_WORKSPACE`. On confirm it removes that window and reopens it with only the requested workspace.\n- If the window is open with incompatible window props, it prompts with `CLOSE_WINDOW` (`explicit: false`, so every workspace in the window is listed). On confirm it replaces that window entry.\n- If the workspace is already open with compatible props, the code restores the window if it's hidden or not the most recent, and returns `true`.\n\n**Other paths.** For a `closable` group, opening a window while other windows are open prompts with `CLOSE_OTHER_WINDOWS` (`workspace2.ts:273-299`). Otherwise the window is appended to `openedWindows` (`workspace2.ts:300-320`).\n\n**Prompt logic.** `promptForClosingWorkspaces` (`workspace2.ts:398`) collects the affected workspaces for each reason and passes them to `showClosePrompt`. Unless the closing is explicit, that function returns `true` without showing a modal when nothing would be lost (`workspace2.ts:363-366`). Only workspaces with unsaved changes count as affected (`getAffectedWorkspacesInWindow`, `workspace2.ts:348`).\n\n**Group close.** `launchWorkspaceGroup2` (`workspace2.ts:32-63`) and `closeWorkspaceGroup2` (`workspace2.ts:74-96`) handle the group-level equivalents. `closeWorkspaceGroup2` prompts only when windows are open, and `discardUnsavedChanges` skips the prompt.\n\n**Not checked:** the `workspace2Store` reducers and the `Workspace2` component that consumes these props live in other files I didn't open. Documentation for `launchWorkspaceGroup2` was only confirmed by a grep match, not read in full.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/workspace2.ts\", \"startLine\": 133, \"endLine\": 321},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/workspace2.ts\", \"startLine\": 98, \"endLine\": 132},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/workspace2.ts\", \"startLine\": 32, \"endLine\": 63},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/workspace2.ts\", \"startLine\": 398, \"endLine\": 430},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/workspace2.ts\", \"startLine\": 323, \"endLine